without DevOps."

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.930
That would probably be
quite appropriate, as well.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.830
So what are we going
to talk about today?

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.670
Well, we're going to talk about
a game called War Dragons.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.080
And thanks, Gustavo, so
much for coming by today

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.190
to talk to us about that.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.535
We really appreciate it.

00:02:08.535 --> 00:02:09.910
So we're going to
go through what

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.520
that game is, have a look
at it, it's pretty awesome.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.020
I like it a lot.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.750
We're going to look at how its
backend infrastructure works.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.350
So obviously this
is a Cloud event.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.100
We want to look at
backend infrastructure.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.900
We want to see what's
going on there.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.160
We're going to talk
about what worked well.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.410
What were the success stories?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.640
What were the great
things that happened?

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.139
And we're also going
to look at some

00:02:31.139 --> 00:02:32.280
of the problems they faced.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.020
What lessons have been learned.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.680
What can we teach
you about building

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.170
backend infrastructures for
this sort of application.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.894
Finally we'll put a bow on
it, reach a nice conclusion,

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.560
and that will be the
